<title>SOUTH KOREA: Miwon buys shares in Sewon.</title>
<headline>Miwon buys shares in Sewon.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Miwon Co Ltd has begun to buy 210,000 common shares of Sewon Co to merge the two companies, a Miwon official said on Friday.</p>
<p>He said the purchase was launched on Thursday and when completed it will bring Miwon's stake in Sewon to 9.94 percent from the current 2.2 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;It aims at merging Sewon with Miwon again,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Sewon, South Korea's largest corn processing firm, split from Miwon in 1994.</p>
<p>Further details were not given.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
</text>
